raw_content:
```yaml
---
id: vuln-dectalk-tts-3600d8ac
pattern-sources:
  - path: src/index.ts
languages:
  - typescript
message: 'HTTP request to dectalk API is insecure. Use HTTPS instead of HTTP.'
severity: ERROR
metadata:
  cve: CVE-2024-31206
  cwe: CWE-300, CWE-319, CWE-598
pattern: |
  import { URL } from 'node:url';
  import { fetch } from 'node:whatwg-fetch';
  import { Buffer } from 'node:buffer';

  export default async function dectalk(text: string): Promise<Buffer> {
    // The API does not like empty prompts
    text = text.trim();
    if (text.length === 0) {
      throw new TypeError('Text cannot be empty or only whitespace');
    }

    const url = new URL('http://tts.cyzon.us/tts');
    // Send request
    const response = await fetch(url);

    // TODO look into custom behavior for aeiou's error codes
    // https://github.com/calzoneman/aeiou/blob/master/docs/usage-guidelines.md
    if (!response.ok) {
      throw new Error(`${response.status} ${response.statusText}`, { cause: response });
    }

    // Parse and return response
    const binaryData = await response.arrayBuffer();
    return Buffer.from(binaryData);
  }
```
This Semgrep rule will detect the use of HTTP URLs in the dectalk function. It will flag this as an ERROR with the message 'HTTP request to dectalk API is insecure. Use HTTPS instead of HTTP.'. The severity is set to ERROR to highlight the potential security risk. The metadata field is used to provide the CVE and CWE numbers. The pattern field is used to match the vulnerable code snippet.

